/-!
# Joint Hessian--Cartan--EC-normal local actual

The KIN-13 coframe Hessian write and the current-native Cartan restart share
the primitive `e`, `B`, and `omega` fields.  This module closes that critical
pair by sending their common output through the already action-generated EC
normal write.  The public constructor consumes only `(source, current)`:

```text
current
  -> action-generated coframe Hessian / Levi--Civita first germ
  -> current-native Cartan connection, computed II+, and live reaction
  -> action-normal curvature connection and recomputed live reaction.
```

The final EC-normal leg preserves the generated coframe field, hence it does
not erase the Hessian dynamics.  It regenerates every field receipt that
depends on the shared connection/reaction actual.  At an identity contact the
same output has simplicity, the auxiliary equation, the full repaired-root
coframe Euler equation, and the Cartan torsion--spin readback simultaneously.

This remains a local/contact producer.  It is not a whole-base stationary
family, a continuous trajectory, a fixed point of the dynamical Hessian
write, or a finite-action receipt.  No residual value, target curvature,
response, equation, branch, phase, or cohomology class is accepted by the
constructor.
-/

